  <th colspan="2" class="Invert">Latest Additions</th>
</tr>
<tr><th class="News">10-18</th><td class="News"><a title="Skorpion OS is a Debian-based Linux distribution with built-in privacy and artificial intelligence (AI) features. It uses Skorpion AI (SKAI), a fully offline AI subsystem powered by Ollama and the Qwen2.5:14B language model. The distribution offers a choice of two user interfaces - a full-featured Cinnamon desktop and a minimalist i3 tiling window manager. Both include the Firefox web browser with a pre-installed SKAI browser extension that employs offline AI only, as well as the Olly desktop assistant designed for interacting with the local filesystem using plain language. Skorpion OS is built for users who view local AI as an essential part of their operating system." href="skorpion">Skorpion OS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">10-17</th><td class="News"><a title="MuliOS is a minimalist, Arch-based Linux distribution featuring the KDE Plasma desktop. It comes with several custom tools, including a system installer called MuliOS Installer, as well as a MuliOS Welcome screen, a MuliOS task manager, and a command-line system update utility called &quot;mupdate&quot;. The distribution provides its own Linux kernel and includes customised boot configuration. MuliOS is designed with a focus on choice, performance, customisation and simplicity." href="mulios">MuliOS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">10-16</th><td class="News"><a title="HoopoeLinux is an Ubuntu-based desktop Linux distribution featuring the Cinnamon desktop. It is developed by Ubuntushop.biz, a Belgium-based company that builds a range of privacy-oriented computers that ship pre-installed with one of the popular Linux distributions, including Ubuntu, Debian, Manjaro, Linux Mint and HoopoeLinux. The distribution comes with several privacy tools, such as AnonSurf (an anonymous mode wrapper to force connections through Tor), Tractor Carburetor (a module for bypassing any VPN ban), Invisible Internet Project (I2P, an encrypted private network layer), and privacy components developed by Kali Linux, Kodachi and Tails. The project also provides its own Tor relay." href="hoopoelinux">HoopoeLinux</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">10-14</th><td class="News"><a title="Lyra OS is a Brazilian desktop and server Linux distribution based on openSUSE Tumbleweed, a rolling-release variant of openSUSE. The desktop edition features a customised GNOME desktop. It provides a simple and intuitive system installer called Lyra Install and a comprehensive control centre termed Vega, which is also available as a command-line and web-based application in Lyra's Server edition. The distribution also ships with LinuxToys, a unified system management, configuration and software installation tool. Lyra OS supports Portuguese (both Brazilian and European) and English languages." href="lyra">Lyra OS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">10-13</th><td class="News"><a title="CarotOS is a specialist Debian-based Linux distribution designed primarily for cybersecurity education in a classroom. It includes a number of security tools, covering network scanning, traffic analysis, web and password testing, and firewall configuration, as well as a number of custom applications, written in Python and released under General Public Licence 3. The principal learning tool is called CarotOS Poligon, a student/teacher application pair for practicing penetration testing in an isolated, local classroom environment. CarotOS boots into a customised Xfce desktop with Turkish as the default language, although English is available for selection either from the Welcome wizard or from the Settings manager, and the application interfaces are available in both languages." href="carotos">CarotOS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">10-12</th><td class="News"><a title="Lightwhale is a independently-developed, minimalist, single-purpose Linux distribution designed to run Docker containers effortlessly. The live ISO image boots directly into a fully functional Docker engine without the need for installation or configuration. The distribution's core system is immutable, while data and customisations are stored entirely separated on a dedicated device. Lightwhale is primarily designed to be deployed on home labs, bare‑metal computers, virtualised environments, edge nodes or clusters." href="lightwhale">Lightwhale</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">10-11</th><td class="News"><a title="Blunux is an Arch-based desktop Linux distribution featuring the KDE Plasma desktop. It offers the Calamares system installer, as well as a large selection of popular KDE applications, such as Calligra office suite, Falkon web browser, K3b disk burning application, KDevelop integrated development environment, KOrganizer personal organiser, KTorrent bittorrent client, and many others. The distribution provides separate images for five supported languages - Simplified Chinese, English, Korean, Spanish and Swedish. Blunux is suitable for users migrating to Linux from other operating systems, bringing a familiar layout with a taskbar, a start menu and an easy-to-use file manager." href="blunux">Blunux</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">10-10</th><td class="News"><a title="ArchiveOS is an Ubuntu-based Linux distribution featuring the KDE Plasma desktop. It is designed primarily for users who are new to Linux. The distribution's principal feature is a collection of graphical ArchiveOS utilities that facilitate various administrative and daily-use tasks; these include DEB Installer, App Remover and Update Manager (for managing DEB, Flatpak and snap software packages), Gaming Center (a game launcher for AppImage, Linux launcher, Windows EXE, Steam and Heroic games), and Windows App Support (for running Windows executable files). ArchiveOS also comes with a comprehensive Welcome app which offers a large range of configuration options, including driver management and system backups." href="archiveos">ArchiveOS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">10-09</th><td class="News"><a title="Anthares OS is a Brazilian desktop Linux distribution based on Debian &quot;Stable&quot;, featuring a highly customised Cinnamon desktop. The project's goal is to provide a lean initial system without any unnecessary software and let the user install extra applications after installation, using a custom-built app store called Unicode Center. It also provides Élise, a proactive and transparent assistant that helps with organising files, setting up a firewall, alerting for software updates, and monitoring privacy violations. Antares OS comes with an intuitive lateral dock for a quick access to notifications and settings, as well as an Android-style application menu with large icons and software categories." href="anthares">Anthares OS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">10-06</th><td class="News"><a title="XXRI OS is an ultra lightweight desktop Linux distribution designed specifically for older and low-specification computers, including 32-bit systems. It features a custom desktop, called XXRI, which strives to be modern and polished, and which does not require the use of terminal for most common tasks. It also provides a set of custom applications, including XXRI Browser, XXRI File and XXRI Media, as well as a comprehensive graphical control centre called XXRI Settings. Although the distribution does not offer any traditional package manager, additional applications can be installed through XXRI Store, an online repository of popular open-source software." href="xxri">XXRI Linux</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">10-04</th><td class="News"><a title="GNUSlashLinux is an Arch-based, rolling-release Linux distribution featuring the minimalist Noctalia desktop shell on top of the niri Wayland compositor. It is designed specifically for developers and power users seeking a lean, keyboard-driven operating system. The distribution's default software set includes a GPU-accelerated Kitty terminal, the modern Helix text editor, the asynchronous Yazi terminal file manager, the privacy-focused Helium web browser, and the Zathura document viewer. GNUSlashLinux also provides several pre-configured themes and colour schemes, as well as various modern command-line tools as alternatives to classic Unix commands." href="gnuslashlinux">GNUSlashLinux</a></td></tr>
</table><br>
