        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px"><a href="funos">FunOS</a>, an Ubuntu-based Linux distribution featuring the lightweight JWM window manager, has been updated to version 26.10. The new release expands the Broadcom wireless support and resolves screen blanking issues: "<span class="Quote">The FunOS team is proud to announce the release of FunOS 26.10, built on top of Ubuntu 26.10 'Stonking Stingray'. This release introduces significant upgrades to core utilities, multimedia handling, and hardware support, while providing a refreshed look and feel. What's New in FunOS 26.10? Based on Ubuntu 26.10 - FunOS 26.10 is built on the robust foundation of Ubuntu 26.10, ensuring access to the latest software packages and improved system performance and modern hardware compatibility; Linux Kernel 7.3 - this release ships with the Linux Kernel 7.3, providing enhanced support for the newest hardware, performance optimizations, updated driver management; 100% Rust core utilities - continuing the focus on security and reliability, FunOS 26.10 completes the transition to using Rust-based core utilities; transition to dbus-broker - FunOS 26.10 moves from dbus-daemon to dbus-broker; transition to PipeWire - we have fully transitioned to PipeWire as the default multimedia server.</span>" Read the rest of the <a href="https://funos.org/funos-26-10/">release announcement</a> for further information. <a href="https://funos.org/download/">Download (MD5)</a>: <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/funos/files/stonking/final/26.10/funos-26.10-stable.20261017.iso">funos-26.10-stable.20261017.iso</a> (2,138MB, <a href="table.php?distribution=funos&pkglist=true&version=26.10#pkglist">pkglist</a>).</td>
