        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px"><a href="ubuntu">Ubuntu Studio</a> is a distribution for creative individuals in the areas of audio production, video production, graphics design, photography and desktop publishing. The project's latest version, 26.10, offers nine months of support and a handful of new tools. "<span class="Quote">Ubuntu Studio’s audio package selections now include Sonic Pi, SuperCollider, and the SuperCollider 3 plugin suite, giving you a complete live-coding and algorithmic-composition toolkit alongside Ardour, Carla, and the rest of the audio stack. Also new is JNoise, a simple white/pink noise generator included purely for its utility, handy for testing audio setups and room or speaker checks. Logo featuring the Greek letter pi on a pink background with decorative curved lines. The inclusion of Sonic Pi was inspired by DJ_Dave, a musician who builds and performs entire tracks as live code. While she currently uses Strudel, a browser-based live-coding environment, similar results can be obtained with Sonic Pi: write a few lines, hear them loop instantly, and keep reshaping the music as it plays. Sonic Pi runs natively on your desktop and is built on top of SuperCollider’s synthesis engine, so you can start with simple loops and samples and grow into deeper sound design.</span>" Additional information can be found in the <a href="https://ubuntustudio.org/2026/10/ubuntu-studio-26-10-released/">release announcement</a> and in the <a href="https://discourse.ubuntu.com/t/ubuntu-studio-26-10-release-notes">release notes</a>. <a href="https://ubuntustudio.org/download/">Download</a>:  <a href="https://cdimage.ubuntu.com/ubuntustudio/releases/stonking/release/ubuntustudio-26.10-desktop-amd64.iso">ubuntustudio-26.10-desktop-amd64.iso</a> (6,585MB, <a href="https://cdimage.ubuntu.com/ubuntustudio/releases/stonking/release/SHA256SUMS">SHA256</a>, <a href="https://cdimage.ubuntu.com/ubuntustudio/releases/stonking/release/SHA256SUMS.gpg">signature</a>, <a href="https://cdimage.ubuntu.com/ubuntustudio/releases/stonking/release/ubuntustudio-26.10-desktop-amd64.iso.torrent">torrent</a>, <a href="table.php?distribution=ubuntustudio&amp;pkglist=true&amp;version=26.10#pkglist">pkglist</a>).</td>
